  "question": {
    "text": "The number of five-digit numbers, greater than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40000</mn></math> and divisible by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math>, which can be formed using the digits <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>7</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn></math> without repetition, is equal to"
  },
  "options": [
